<title>ITALY: BNL H1 net profit climbs to 46 bln lire.</title>
<headline>BNL H1 net profit climbs to 46 bln lire.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30.</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Parent net profit		     46 vs   42</p>
<p>    Parent pre-tax profit		 74 vs   67</p>
<p>    Consolidated net profit	     98 vs   61</p>
<p>    Consolidated pre-tax profit	241 vs  114</p>
<p>Note: Full name Banca Nazionale del Lavoro (BNL).  </p>
<p>    Parent interest margin	   1,440 vs   1,498</p>
<p>    Parent intermediary margins    2,180 vs   2,128</p>
<p>    Parent operating result	    586 vs     609</p>
<p>    Total parent loans	     128,010 vs 128,706</p>
<p>    Parent client loans	     84,762 vs  84,049</p>
<p>    Total parent deposits	  123,811 vs 121,964</p>
<p>    Parent client deposits	  76,210 vs  70,049</p>
<p>Note: BNL chairman Sarcinelli said in a statement the results showed the group moving increasingly towards services and dealing.  </p>
<p>BNL said parent company bad loans equalled 2.003 billion lire -- 2.36 percent of all client loans. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
